From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:44:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add LICENSE matching setuptools' default license_files glob

setuptools only auto-discovers license files at the project root that
match LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS*. The project declares itself MIT
in pyproject.toml's classifiers (License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License) and
on PyPI, but ships no LICENSE file anywhere in the tree or in the published
wheel's dist-info (checked vtzero-0.0.1b5-cp310-cp310-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
directly: only WHEEL/RECORD/top_level.txt/METADATA), so no license text at
all reaches dist-info/licenses/.

Add the canonical MIT text (attributed to the project's sole author, Yohan
Boniface, per setup.py) so it is picked up by the default glob with no
setup.cfg/setup.py change.

Also add LICENSE.vtzero and LICENSE.protozero, reproducing mapbox/vtzero and
mapbox/protozero's own BSD license texts verbatim at the exact commits this
release's vendor/vtzero and vendor/protozero submodules are pinned to
(67f934ee9aa44b923b5d0bc2bc87448900051a57 and
542fcf7dd228672b775eb283d18ccd94c4e682d9) -- their header-only C++ sources are
compiled directly into the vtzero.tile extension, and the same default glob
picks these up too.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [blocked: this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]
---
 LICENSE           | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.protozero | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.vtzero    | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 70 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.protozero
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.vtzero

